    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="1670" n="1630" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/8–2054: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 875<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Israel</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d875-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-26T19:02:00-04:00">August 26, 1954—7:02
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. Amman’s 60<anchor n="2" xml:id="d875-f2"/> Tel Aviv’s 192<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d875-f3"/> Cairo’s 203.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d875-f4"/> Tel Aviv
                    requested approach Dayan reporting that
                    our initial soundings in Cairo and Amman indicate willingness for commanders to
                    meet. We suggest first meetings be held between commanders Jlem sector and Gaza frontiers. In our view agenda
                    should be limited discussion border security measures and to setting up means
                    for further periodic contacts with view reduction border incidents. Arrangements
                    could be made regarding place and time meeting through UNTSO observers. It should be made clear that what we are seeking
                    is resumption commanders meetings which as in past would be held informally and
                    outside framework MAC. FYI while we would hope such meetings might improve atmosphere to
                    degree where Israel would see value resuming full cooperation with MAC feel would be counter-productive attempt link
                    these meetings with MAC participation at this
                    time.</p>
                <p>Tel Aviv requested consult closely with ConGen
                    Jlem and at appropriate time ConGen should provide background to UNTSO.</p>
                <p>Cairo and Amman requested make similar approaches Gohar and Arab Legion.</p>
                <p>Report developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
